    description: "FOUND 2026-10-24 while checking WI-popak's trigger (INV-kurup, stage 10). The schema-coverage corpus has 0 violations on default and include_docs (VALIDATION_BASELINES still say 11). Real-repo surveys (jahuf_10232026 AFTER arms, dev 2aeec80eb3 code) still carry the id-format:F3 advisory kind-slot class (kind-slot not registered / != Symbol.kind), all from three producers that put a ROLE in the id's kind slot:\n  - cuda.py: the id discriminator is cuda_execution_space (device / global / host / host_device), while kind=\"function\" and the meta already carries the space. whisper.cpp: 698 device + 238 global + 34 host + 28 host_device symbols (x2 violations each).\n  - xml_config.py, AndroidManifest components: the kind slot is the element name (activity / service / receiver / provider), while kind=\"component\" and meta.component_type carries it. sherpa-onnx 42, grpc 4, whisper.cpp 4.\n  - linkers/message_dispatch.py: f-string ids ending :message_sender / :message_handler on kind=\"function\" nodes (meta.framework_role carries it). sherpa-onnx 26, whisper.cpp 14. The ids are also hand-built f-strings, not make_symbol_id (WI-vodin's linker did not reach them).\nFIX: the kind slot is the kind (ADR-0036; WI-kugaj's precedent for route/event). Node ids change, stable_ids do not: each producer's stable_id already hashes kind=\"function\"/\"component\" (verify per producer). A same-location sender/handler pair would collide only if one line were both a send and a handle site. Acceptance: those surveys show 0 kind-slot advisories from these producers; WI-popak can then flip."  # b1b6
